created {'thresholds': {'seed': 42, 'instance': 21, 'ros_domain_id': 71, 'agent_port': 18888, 'startup_timeout_s': 90, 'takeoff_timeout_s': 45, 'landing_timeout_s': 60, 'hover_s': 10, 'neural_s': 5, 'repetitions': 3, 'altitude_m': 3, 'hover_max_error_m': 1.0, 'hover_max_tilt_deg': 15, 'safety_radius_m': 10, 'safety_altitude_m': 8, 'safety_tilt_deg': 45, 'safety_angular_rate_rad_s': 8, 'inference_p99_us': 2500, 'settling_band_m': 0.2, 'settling_dwell_s': 2.0, 'joint_recovery': {'position_reference': 'active_controller_target', 'position_reference_note': "Same rule as P0 (the controller's own position target), extended to RAPTOR: its internal target is not published on trajectory_setpoint, so while RAPTOR owns the actuators the target is its logged capture (activation reset or setpoint-stale hold); classic stages use trajectory_setpoint as in P0. trajectory_setpoint-only and fixed NED results are kept as comparisons.", 'position_reference_ned_m': [0, 0, -3], 'velocity_reference_ned_m_s': [0, 0, 0], 'angular_velocity_reference_frd_rad_s': [0, 0, 0], 'position_threshold_m': 0.2, 'velocity_threshold_m_s': 0.1, 'angular_velocity_threshold_rad_s': 0.1, 'dwell_s': 2.0, 'max_observation_gap_s': 0.02}, 'p0_strict': True, 'p2': {'purpose': 'P2 internal-state treatments at RAPTOR takeover (C->N) and velocity-integrator coordination at classic takeover (N->C). RAPTOR activation target capture (current position/yaw, zero velocity) is unchanged; only the GRU hidden state and previous action are written.', 'conditions': {'S1': {'speed_m_s': 0.0, 'description': 'stable hover (P1 S1)'}, 'S3': {'speed_m_s': 1.0, 'raptor_baseline_speed_m_s': 1.0, 'description': '1.0 m/s along +N (P1 S3). raptor_baseline_speed_m_s is calibrated by development runs so that the RAPTOR baseline capture speed lies in 1.00-1.04 m/s like the C->N handovers.'}, 'X1.5': {'speed_m_s': 1.5, 'start_offset_m': -6.0, 'cruise_s': 1.5, 'description': 'exploration'}, 'X2.0': {'speed_m_s': 2.0, 'start_offset_m': -6.0, 'cruise_s': 1.5, 'description': 'exploration'}, 'X2.5': {'speed_m_s': 2.5, 'start_offset_m': -6.0, 'cruise_s': 1.5, 'description': 'exploration'}, 'X3.0': {'speed_m_s': 3.0, 'start_offset_m': -6.0, 'cruise_s': 1.5, 'description': 'exploration'}}, 'profile_overrides': ['start_offset_m', 'cruise_s', 'accel_s', 'reference_hold_s'], 'exploration_rationale': 'Exploration conditions first move 6 m back along -N at 0.5 m/s (trapezoid, 0.5 m/s^2) and hold 3 s, then ramp for 2 s and cruise 1.5 s, so that 3.0 m/s reaches the trigger near +1.5 m and leaves more than 8 m to the frozen 10 m safety radius for braking.', 'treatments': {'N0': {'rini': 0, 'description': 'original RAPTOR mode-entry reset'}, 'N1': {'rini': 2, 'description': 'GRU reset; previous action = classic last applied actuator_motors in RAPTOR action space'}, 'N2g': {'rini': 3, 'description': 'while inactive the shadow inference sees classic applied motors as previous action (teacher forcing); entry keeps the GRU, previous action reset'}, 'N2': {'rini': 4, 'description': 'teacher forcing as N2g; entry keeps the GRU and sets previous action = classic last applied motors'}, 'N2s': {'rini': 1, 'description': 'pre-existing RINI=1: keep the shadow inference memory (own shadow actions)'}, 'Nstar': {'rini': 5, 'description': 'S1 only: staged GRU and previous action of a RAPTOR S1 baseline at the same phase (upper bound)'}, 'C0': {'nco': 0, 'description': 'original classic AUTO_LOITER takeover'}, 'C2': {'nco': 1, 'description': 'classic velocity integrator coordinated with RAPTOR last applied collective thrust along the current body z axis'}, 'B': {'rini': 0, 'nco': 0, 'description': 'same-controller baseline, no treatment'}}, 'nstar_memory': {'values': None, 'source': None, 'note': 'GRU[16] + previous action[4], filled from a development RAPTOR S1 baseline before the S1 batch is frozen'}, 'motion_axis_ned': [1, 0, 0], 'reference_hold_s': 3.0, 'accel_s': 2.0, 'cruise_s': 4.0, 'offboard_prestream_s': 1.0, 'setpoint_period_s': 0.02, 'post_handover_s': 10.0, 'return_hold_s': 8.0, 'reposition': {'speed_m_s': 0.5, 'accel_m_s2': 0.5}, 'reference': 'Before the subject event the outgoing controller tracks one runner-published trajectory_setpoint (position ramp, velocity and acceleration feed-forward, constant yaw) starting from its own current target: classic through OFFBOARD, RAPTOR through its external trajectory_setpoint input. At the event the stream stops and the incoming controller uses its original mechanism: RAPTOR mode-entry reset holds the activation position/yaw with zero velocity; classic AUTO_LOITER brakes to the navigator loiter point.', 'baselines': "p1_baseline_classic: classic OFFBOARD motion then AUTO_LOITER (same takeover mechanism, no controller switch). p1_baseline_raptor: RAPTOR external-setpoint motion then the stream stops; after RAPTOR's 200 ms setpoint timeout it holds its position (same capture rule as mode entry, no reset or switch).", 'motor_saturation': {'upper': 0.999, 'lower': 0.001, 'note': 'actuator_motors control in [0,1]; upper/lower limit within 1e-3'}, 'motor_step_window_s': [-0.1, 0.5], 'motor_rms_window_s': [0.0, 0.5], 'motor_rms_definition': "RMS over [change, change+0.5 s] and the four motors of (run actuator_motors - in-batch baseline mean curve), zero-order hold on a 1 ms grid aligned at each run's actual change; baseline = same-controller baseline of the same condition in the same batch.", 'elimination_ratio_definition': '(N0 - Nx) / (N0 - baseline) per metric, from in-batch group means (motor step at change, max altitude loss, motor RMS deviation).', 'entry_check': {'value_tolerance': 1e-05, 'classic_command_max_age_ms': 50, 'teacher_forcing_check_window_s': 1.0, 'teacher_forced_min_fraction': 0.99}, 'exploration': {'failure_criteria': {'safety_envelope': 'any of tilt >= 45 deg, angular-rate component >= 8 rad/s, horizontal radius >= 10 m, altitude >= 8 m (frozen safety envelope; reaching the limit counts), or a runner safety abort', 'no_joint_